The file gate.lisp holds a define-owner form for a counting gate. A close
on a gate opened more than once must step the count down instead of matching
nothing. Append ONE new clause, as the LAST clause:

  (:transition ((:open ?count) (:close))
    :when (> ?count 1)
    => `(:open ,(1- ?count))
    (list :publish :gate.stepped (1- ?count)))

Note the backquote and unquote — the new state interpolates (1- ?count). The
existing clauses must be untouched and their order preserved. ./check must
exit 0.